    "updated_at": "2022-05-10T09:57:42Z",
    "body": "With this PR I'm trying to unblock the discussion ongoing in the [PR#5482](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/5482) where we are trying to add several dweb protocols to the scheme safelist. During the discussion in the Firefox standard-position request, it was [suggested](https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/339#issuecomment-644289267) to split up the PR to analyze each protocol independently, to address the concern of endorsing the technologies behind the schemes. \r\n\r\nI guess we can assume Chrome's support given that a [CL](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/2153064) has already landed upstream with all these schemes safelisted. \r\n\r\nRegarding Firefox, as mentioned before, there is an ongoing discussion in the standatd-postiion [request](https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/339) submitted for the PR#5482, but perhaps we would need a new one specifically about IPFS and IPNS, as suggested by @dbaron \r\n\r\nThere is already a tentative test in the WPT repository, with all the protocols. We can merge it with the test defined for the current safelist schemes once this PR is merged.",
